# What `vercel deploy` must not upload.
#
# Needed because the CLI uploads the working directory as it finds it and does
# not read .gitignore. A deployment built from a Git push never sees any of
# this; a CLI deploy would otherwise spend minutes pushing 189MB of archived
# Instagram media the build has no use for.

# The archived originals. Local working material for the import scripts, which
# run from a committee member's machine and never on Vercel. The manifests
# beside them are small, are committed, and are deliberately not excluded.
scripts/data/instagram/*.jpg
scripts/data/instagram/*.mp4

# The raw scrape those were taken from.
dataset_instagram-scraper_*.json

# Screenshots left at the root. Named one by one rather than as *.png: the
# site's own images are PNGs too, and public/logo.png holds the space on every
# event card without a poster.
/03-events-mobile.png
/04-events-mobile-scrolled.png
/05-events-big.png
